{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T02:35:28.443Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019fd4ec-fb3b-72e3-b83e-85984acf7b23","author":"/root/final_verification_matrix","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/final_verification_matrix\nPayload:\nRead-only audit complete; I changed no files, refs, containers, or remotes.\n\nCritical compliance point: submitting 99 draft PRs triggers `PR Quality` for every PR, with no draft exemption. The documented local-first rule applies to the exact commit being pushed. Therefore, a single green run at the stack tip proves only the integrated result—not all 99 rewritten predecessor heads. Literal compliance requires the normal PR gate at every final branch head, or an explicit policy exception. See [PR workflow](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.github/workflows/pr-quality.yml:3) and [local-first rule](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:239).\n\n## Ordered validation matrix\n\n1. Structural gate before testing:\n\n   - Exactly 99 branches; a 100th is a failure.\n   - Every PR changes fewer than 100 files.\n   - Keep the sole approved size exception limited to the one-file generated legacy-snapshot deletion.\n   - Resolve subject ambiguities flagged by the manifest audit: uppercase `QR`, uppercase `Scaleway`, and whether `infra:` is accepted as a conventional type.\n   - No dirty tree, pending restack, or `needsRebase`.\n\n2. Prerequisites:\n\n```bash\nexport APP_HOST_PORT=4200\nbun install --frozen-lockfile\nbun run test:e2e:install\n```\n\n   Port 4200 must be free or owned by this exact checkout because Auth0 callbacks are configured externally. Tool baselines are Bun 1.3.14, Node 24.15.0, Docker Compose 2.24+, PostgreSQL 17, and Playwright Chromium. See [README.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/README.md:5), [tests/README.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:246), and [Playwright installation](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:378).\n\n3. Static, unit, build, Terraform, and image gate—repeat at every final PR head:\n\n```bash\nbun run release:validate\nbun run format:write\nbun run format:check\nbun run lint\nactionlint .github/workflows/*.yml\nbash -n helpers/testing/docker-resume.sh helpers/testing/docker-stack.sh helpers/testing/docker-webserver.sh\ngit diff --check origin/main...HEAD\ngit diff --exit-code\ntest -z \"$(git status --porcelain=v1)\"\n\nbun run test:unit:server\nCI=true bun run test:unit\nbun run build:app\nbun run infra:check\nbun run image:security:local\n```\n\n   If formatting or lint changes anything, stop, commit/restack, and restart validation. `infra:check` performs Terraform formatting, init/validation for all three roots, and Trivy configuration scanning. `image:security:local` builds Linux/amd64, checks runtime shape/size, exports source maps, generates an SBOM, and scans HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities. See [README gate](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/README.md:97), [Terraform verifier](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/ops/scaleway/verify-terraform.sh:12), and [image verifier](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/ops/scaleway/verify-image-security.sh:20).\n\n4. Project-scoped Docker reset and PostgreSQL proof—repeat per PR head:\n\n```bash\nbun run env:runtime\nbun run docker:check\n\nnode_modules/.bin/dotenv -c dev -- \\\n  bun helpers/testing/run-with-wall-clock-timeout.ts 90 2 \\\n  docker compose down --timeout 60 --remove-orphans --volumes\n\nbun run docker:start\nbun run docker:ps\n\ntest \"$(curl --silent --show-error --output /dev/null \\\n  --write-out '%{http_code}' http://localhost:4200/readyz)\" = 204\n\nbun run test:integration:postgres:local\n\nnode_modules/.bin/dotenv -c dev -- \\\n  bun helpers/testing/run-with-wall-clock-timeout.ts 90 2 \\\n  docker compose down --timeout 60 --remove-orphans --volumes\n```\n\n   Run this only after the pending bounded-Docker layer is committed; the current source still has potentially unbounded `down && up --build` scripts. The teardown remains isolated through generated `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`; never use system-wide prune. The PostgreSQL runner resets only the named loopback `evorto_postgres_integration` database and rejects remote targets. See [runtime isolation](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/runtime-environment.ts:154), [PostgreSQL contract](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:178), and [Docker ownership](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:284).\n\n5. Complete Playwright baseline—repeat at every PR head under the documented normal PR baseline:\n\n```bash\nbun run test:e2e\nbun run test:e2e:docs\n```\n\n   Start with no unknown server on port 4200. Let Playwright own a fresh stack, or explicitly prove the running stack was built from that exact head. Both commands must have zero failures, skips, todos, fixmes, expected failures, retries/flakes, interruptions, or focused tests. See [README.md](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/README.md:117), [completeness rule](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:251), and [Playwright server ownership](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/playwright.config.ts:82).\n\n6. Provider certification—at minimum on the final integrated tip and every head that changes provider behavior:\n\n```bash\nbun run test:e2e:integration\nbun run test:e2e:live-esncard:release\n```\n\n   Run in that order. The first includes functional and generated-doc Auth0 Management/Google Maps projects. The second includes the provider-error unit test plus active-card, expired-card, and generated-doc ESNcard journeys. The shorter `test:e2e:live-esncard` command is insufficient. See [provider gate](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:260) and [suite composition](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/tests/README.md:309).\n\n7. Browser-only proof on the final integrated tip:\n\n   Use the Codex in-app Browser for discovery and announcement visibility, participant registration/profile, organizer authoring/scanning, tenant administration/finance, and platform administration. Record the path, visible result, console/network state, and screenshots where useful.\n\n   Playwright, screenshots, system Chrome, and `test:e2e:ui` do not substitute for this walkthrough. If Browser control is unavailable, record it as a blocker. See [Browser distinction](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:52), [manual queue](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:197), and [evidence rules](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/QUALITY.md:357).\n\n## Credentials and external dependencies\n\n- All Docker/Playwright: `FONT_AWESOME_TOKEN`, `CLIENT_ID`, `CLIENT_SECRET`, `ISSUER_BASE_URL`, `SECRET` of at least 32 bytes, Stripe test-mode API key/account, and all six non-production Auth0 account passwords.\n- Integration: `AUTH0_MANAGEMENT_CLIENT_ID`, `AUTH0_MANAGEMENT_CLIENT_SECRET`, `PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY`.\n- Live provider: approved active and permanently expired ESNcard identifiers.\n- Infrastructure/image: internet access for pinned Terraform, Trivy, Syft, providers, vulnerability databases, Docker images, and package registries; no Scaleway production credentials are needed.\n- Docker provides local MinIO and a file-backed Stripe webhook secret.\n\nThe authoritative variable list is in [.env.example](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/.env.example:4) and [runtime preflight](/Users/hedde/.codex/worktrees/17cb/evorto/helpers/testing/runtime-preflight.ts:47).\n\n## Commands not to count as final evidence\n\n- Bare `bun run test:unit` in a local TTY can enter watch mode; use `CI=true bun run test:unit`.\n- `dev:start`, `build:watch`, `docker:start:watch`, `docker:start:foreground`, `docker:webserver`, `test:e2e:ui`, `test:e2e:report`, and `db:studio` are interactive or long-running.\n- Forwarded files, filters, projects, grep, shards, changed/related selectors, or reporter overrides are diagnostic only.\n- `test:e2e:docs:publish` mutates the separate Evorto Pages checkout and is not a pre-submit gate; baseline, integration, and live documentation are already covered by the commands above.\n- Staging reset/deployment, production promotion, and release publication workflows are external mutations and do not run for draft PR submission."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
