urn vulnerability notes, disclosure reports, PoCs, source code, or Codex Securit (file: r5/vulnerability-writeup/SKILL.md)\n- computer-use:computer-use: Control local Mac apps through Computer Use for tasks that require reading or ope (file: r3/computer-use/1.0.1000550/skills/computer-use/SKILL.md)\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted d (file: r12/documents/26.802.11031/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- effect-best-practices: Enforces Effect-TS patterns for services, errors, layers, and atoms. Use when wr (file: r1/effect-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n- email-best-practices: Use when building email features, emails going to spam, high bounce rates, setting (file: r1/email-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n- explain: Explains the intent behind source code by finding original session transcripts.  (file: r1/explain/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-code-connect: Creates and maintains Figma Code Connect template files that map Figma component (file: r6/figma-code-connect/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-create-new-file: **MANDATORY prerequisite** — you MUST invoke this skill BEFORE every `create_new (file: r6/figma-create-new-file/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-design-to-code: **MANDATORY prerequisite** — you MUST invoke this skill BEFORE calling the `get_de (file: r6/figma-design-to-code/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-generate-design: Use this skill alongside figma-use when the task involves translating an applicati (file: r6/figma-generate-design/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-generate-diagram: MANDATORY prerequisite — load this skill BEFORE every `generate_diagram` tool call (file: r6/figma-generate-diagram/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-generate-library: Build or update a professional-grade design system in Figma from a codebase. Use (file: r6/figma-generate-library/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-implement-motion: Translates Figma motion and animations into production-ready application code. U (file: r6/figma-implement-motion/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-swiftui: SwiftUI ↔ Figma translation. Use whenever the user mentions Swift, SwiftUI, iOS, (file: r6/figma-swiftui/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use: **MANDATORY prerequisite** — you MUST invoke this skill BEFORE every `use_figma` (file: r6/figma-use/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use-figjam: This skill helps agents use Figma's use_figma MCP tool in the FigJam context. Ca (file: r6/figma-use-figjam/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use-motion: Motion / animation context for the `use_figma` MCP tool — animating Figma nodes vi (file: r6/figma-use-motion/SKILL.md)\n- figma:figma-use-slides: This skill helps agents use Figma's use_figma MCP tool in the Slides context. Ca (file: r6/figma-use-slides/SKILL.md)\n- find-skills: Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how  (file: r1/find-skills/SKILL.md)\n- gh-stack: Manages stacked PRs and splits multi-part work into reviewable branches with gh-st (file: r1/gh-stack/SKILL.md)\n- gmail:gmail: Manage Gmail search, thread reading, summaries, reply or forward drafts, self-d (file: r7/gmail/0.1.6/skills/gmail/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar: Manage scheduling and conflicts in connected Google Calendar data. Use when the  (file: r8/google-calendar/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-daily-brief: Build polished one-day Google Calendar briefs. Use when the user asks for today, (file: r8/google-calendar-daily-brief/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-free-up-time: Find ways to open up meaningful free time in a connected Google Calendar. Use when (file: r8/google-calendar-free-up-time/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-group-scheduler: Find and rank good meeting times for multiple people using connected Google Cale (file: r8/google-calendar-group-scheduler/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-meeting-prep: Build a practical meeting prep brief from a connected Google Calendar event and it (file: r8/google-calendar-meeting-prep/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-docs: Prompt- and templa