{"timestamp":"2026-08-06T05:38:29.622Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019fd594-8a76-74d1-ba9d-55c98599749a","call_id":"call_C2n4A7yHJlmMIo9ZzYbPRly5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"13:`c5747a9532ce67fb79f4f379598d161c2e4dc005`, tree\n14:`dfad7e748ff9f8b23698c8263bf4eb90b07c5aba`. It records the intended final\n15:99-layer stack shape without inventing a position-95 or final position-99\n24:| 94        | Bounded local Docker lifecycle                                                 | `c5747a9532ce67fb79f4f379598d161c2e4dc005`, tree `dfad7e748ff9f8b23698c8263bf4eb90b07c5aba`                                                                                                                           |\n25:| 95        | This review queue                                                              | One new file only; commit and tree intentionally remain unrecorded until the patch is applied                                                                                                                         |\n26:| 96-99     | Request tracing, bounded staging probe, automated evidence, and response guide | Four focused patches are prepared and replay cleanly after the position-94 tree; their final shared commits must be created only after position 95                                                                    |\n82:| RQ-001 | Complete       | Historical ledgers, the legacy importer and schema tree, migration-only tests, and obsolete deployment-data scripts remain deleted in the reconstructed prefix                                      | Confirm the same deletions in the final 99-layer diff                                                                                         |\n92:| RQ-011 | In progress    | Position 94 bounds every ordinary Compose operation, reports project state, and removes teardown retry behavior; shell syntax and 45 focused Vitest tests pass                                      | Real project-scoped start/stop/status/resume/readiness, infrastructure validation, and image-security proof on the unchanged final tree       |\n96:| RQ-015 | In progress    | The exact 94-layer executable/documentation prefix is structurally assembled; UI full suites and the final Docker focused suite are green                                                           | Apply positions 95-99, audit exactly 99 heads, then complete every canonical per-head and final integrated environment gate listed below      |\n120:| RQ-015 | Final verification          | Lint, format, build, unit, integration, image security, Playwright, Browser acceptance | Complete | Frozen local install, format, lint, both explicit type checks, production build, release validation, Terraform bootstrap/production/staging with zero misconfigurations, 144-file/1,106-test Angular, 199-file/1,603-test server, 17-file/83-test PostgreSQL, 153/153 functional, 11/11 integration, 54/54 provider-backed guide publication, 8-focused-unit-check/9-journey live ESNcard certification, verified Pages output, and branch-authentic Browser checks pass. The 95,726,857-byte linux/amd64 runtime image contains no source maps; they were exported separately, and the final image check found zero vulnerabilities. The user-cancelled repository scan was not restarted.                 |\n167:| F-095 | Medium   | Accepted tenant configuration did not directly apply its document theme class, while `index.html` advertised two static browser colors that matched none of the available palettes    | Apply exactly one current theme class through the shared tenant-configuration path and delete the invalid static `theme-color` tags; add no dynamic mapping subsystem | Resolved |\n338:| F-158 | Medium   | Ordinary Docker commands could wait indefinitely on Compose inspection/start/stop calls, while Playwright-owned teardown retried a failed or incomplete cleanup and could mask the first actionable failure | Put one wall-clock bound around each operation, stop on the first failure with project state and recent logs, verify owned cleanup once, and never retry or silently rebuild a partial stack | Resolved in source and focused proof at position 94: 8 files, +479/-141; shell syntax and 45/45 focused Vitest tests pass. Real Docker lifecycle, readiness, and image evidence remains explicitly open under RQ-011 and RQ-015 |\n381:| C-032 | Bun/Angular reported-Node compatibility define                             | Angular 22 rejects Bun 1.3.14's reported Node version, so every Angular CLI command rewrites `process.version` and `process.versions.node`                                                 | Keep the explicit define only on Bun 1.3.14; after [Node compatibility commit `0fcead6`](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/commit/0fcead62d8df317ca62b15cd2d6ad185f7639d59) and [Angular coverage commit `749589f`](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/commit/749589fe798fd078d473b0f093ede73289e0de22) ship in stable, update and delete the define/docs | Strong          | Accepted: 1.3.14 is the latest stable; canary is not an acceptable production baseline                                                                                                                      |\n412:  change](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/commit/749589fe798fd078d473b0f093ede73289e0de22);\n466:describes the superseded reference tree, not the reconstructed 99-layer stack.\n695:- 2026-07-27: Added the requested `#4956C8` / `#62677A` / `#FFB26B` /\n729:  exact image gate now passes at 95,685,275 bytes with zero High/Critical\n737:  validation, formatting, lint, clean-tree checks, server 1,495/1,495, Angular\n738:  956/956, PostgreSQL 68/68, build, Terraform/Trivy, the exact 95,685,275-byte\n1020:  built the 95,726,857-byte linux/amd64 image, excluded runtime source maps,\n1039:### Reconstructed 99-layer stack checkpoint\n1060:- 2026-08-05: Added F-158 at position 94. Ordinary start, stop, status, resume,\n1066:- 2026-08-05: Prepared this queue as the sole position-95 file and independently\n1070:  absent until position 95 exists.\n1083:  `c5747a9532ce67fb79f4f379598d161c2e4dc005`, with exactly one intended branch\n1091:- Position 94: 8 files, +479/-141; shell syntax, diff check, and the configured\n1104:- Create positions 95-99, then prove exactly 99 first-parent commits and one\n1130:must not be read as proof for the reconstructed 99-layer stack.\n1228:- Current `image:security:local` gate: the 95,726,857-byte linux/amd64 runtime\n1293:- the one-file position-95 patch and four prepared latency layers to produce\n1305:  pre-position-95 checkpoint.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fd2d8-aa27-7b33-9da1-34e7e79b653d"}}}
